Cascadia: every edit to an existing kernel file, as one patch.

Generated from the working tree against the pinned v6.12 with:

    git diff -- <the files below>      (excluding files corrupted by macOS's
                                        case-insensitive filesystem -- see below)

This replaces the anchor-matching that scripts/apply-p105-boot-hacks.py did.
Anchors were a reasonable idea when the kernel version floated, and a liability
once it was pinned: a missed anchor was SKIPPED, not reported, so a clean tree
built green and booted with no interrupts at all -- init/main.c is where
apple_aic1_rearm() lives, and it was the first thing to go missing.  A patch
either applies or says why.

Not included, deliberately: net/netfilter/xt_{DSCP,HL,TCPMSS,RATEEST}.c,
include/uapi/linux/netfilter*/*.h and one litmus test.  Those show as modified
in the author's tree because macOS's filesystem is case-insensitive and
xt_DSCP.c and xt_dscp.c are the same name to it, so git checks one out over the
other.  They are not our changes and none of them is built here.

kernel/fork.c carries only p105_fb_dbg() stamps left from debugging the init
hang.  They cost nothing and they are how that hang was found; drop them when
the framebuffer debug path goes.

